WEBVTT

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.280
Prepare yourself, Boy Detective Tatekawa!

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.760
I'm laaaaate!!!

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.230
Huh?

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:05.020
Ah, it's Hadzuki-chan!

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.600
Hey, Hadzuki-chan!

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.440
Good morning...

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:19.960
A Liar's First Friendship.

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:30.630
Hey hey, if I use magic, I won't be late for school anymore.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:32.880
What if someone sees you?

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.880
I hadn't thought of that...

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:43.180
Nobuko-chan, good morning!

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:44.950
No!

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:47.850
From now on, school regulations say we can't greet each other!

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:49.660
Eh? No way!

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:51.310
Gotcha.

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:54.230
Hadzuki-chan, you're still so naïve.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:57.690
Seeing as Nobuko-chan could trick you like that.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.130
By the way, Doremi-chan, you're pretty famous.

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:02.030
Why is that?

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:06.370
Class rumor has it that you've been getting prettier lately.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.120
Ehh? Really?

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.580
It's true.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.960
Kotake and the SOS said so yesterday in the locker room.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.000
They said your hairdo is really cute.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:19.670
Is that so?

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:21.590
Doremi-chan.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:23.380
Look!

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.360
Oh no...

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:29.980
She did it again...

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:38.940
Here...

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.490
Mad Majo Rika, always angry.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:12.680
And then... The look on Norihiro's face...

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:15.020
Norihiro? Who's Norihiro?

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.240
Oh, from that idol group.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:19.730
What? From the Wonderfuls?

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:21.830
Right, the Wonderfuls.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:23.280
No way!

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.570
Eh? What?

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:27.370
Ain't the pretty one Yutaka-kun?

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.660
Oh, I prefer Yukio-sama.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:32.040
You're all so naïve.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.170
Nobuko-chan.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:35.670
Whaddya mean, naïve?

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:36.790
Didn't you know?

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:39.420
Norihiro is a cheapskate. Yutaka has a mother complex.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.550
And Yukio sews in his spare time.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.550
Heeeh, ya know 'em pretty well.

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:45.510
But how do ya know stuff like that?

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:49.640
Because... I'm Yutaka's relative.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.140
Wow, then ya can get his autograph!

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:57.100
Of course. If I want his autograph or seal, all I have to do is ask.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.730
How wonderful...

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:00.570
Shall I get it for you?

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:01.820
Wow, really?

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:02.860
Sure, sure.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:06.290
Yay! Thank you! Thanks, thanks!

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:08.200
That's great.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.990
And you must be... Yokokawa...

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:12.120
Nobuko.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.710
Nobuko! Right, Nobu-chan.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:19.500
From this moment on, I'll be yer best friend, Nobu-chan.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:21.650
Best friend?

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:22.800
Yeah.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:23.590
Really?

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.440
Would I lie to you?

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:27.590
Now then, please get me that autograph.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:28.840
Sure.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:34.850
A lie?

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:39.420
Yeah, we felt sorry for her, so we didn't say anything.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:43.030
Yes! Because Nobuko-chan is a total showoff.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:45.190
A total showoff?

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:48.570
Before, she said she had Miyuki the manga artist's autograph.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:51.970
And before that, she said she was friends with the President of the United States.

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:54.410
But no one got their autographs.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:59.370
But her stories are so interesting you can't help but listen.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.750
My mom loves her adventure stories.

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:05.920
I prefer the story of the wounded man.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.760
You mean the drunk man?

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.090
Come on!

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:16.930
Yokokawa-san, aren't you gonna eat your carrots?

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.780
Actually, I'd like to.

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:23.900
But my grandfather told me not to eat carrots ever.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:26.110
Really?

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:27.700
Really.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:32.070
Yes, it was when my grandfather was young.

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:35.790
That winter night, a young woman appeared at the door.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:43.290
It was a very cold night, so he invited her in and prepared a carrot stew.

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:46.630
What's wrong, Miss?

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:49.970
I'm sorry, I can't eat carrots.

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:51.870
How come? Why?

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:55.430
Because... I'm a carrot!

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:59.850
My destiny is to be eaten by a man as kind as you.

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:00.900
Please eat me.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:04.110
How... How could I eat you now?

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:07.230
You really are a kind man!

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.420
Carrot...

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:10.740
Ahh... Carrot...

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:13.620
And both of them lived happily ever after.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:15.160
Happy ending, happy ending!

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:19.330
So your grandmother was a carrot, Yokokawa-san.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:23.210
Er... you could put it that way...

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:25.630
That's amazing.

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:35.760
Hey, Yokokawa-san. Stop being lazy and help me out a little!

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.220
You're on duty too.

00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:42.440
I feel dizzy all of a sudden...

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:44.650
Don't say that while holding your stomach!

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:46.920
Reika-chan, didn't you know?

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:48.020
Know what?

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:51.320
Dizziness is caused by the stomach's DNA.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:52.070
Liar.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:53.570
I'm not lying.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:58.700
DNA stands for "always causing trouble somehow."

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.500
She keeps tellin' lies.

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:07.290
But they're still pretty funny.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.160
W-W-What are you looking at?

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:26.960
Whatcha writin' about?

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:28.440
N-None of your business.

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.480
Why're ya gettin' so nervous?

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:33.820
Don't tell me yer writin' a love letter?

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.740
No, no! How could I do such a thing?

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:40.410
By the way, Aiko-chan, about the autograph...

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:43.910
Ah, that? No hurry.

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:47.710
There's no problem. My mom works at the TV station.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:49.710
So if I ask my mom...

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.170
Ain't he yer relative?

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:52.760
Y-yeah, that's right.

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:55.800
My mom's position is pretty high at the TV station.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:09:00.720
Oh yeah, Yutaka got his debut because of my mom.

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:04.140
She asked me if I wanted to go along that time.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:08.230
Hmm, Nobu-chan, so yer mom works at the TV station.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.690
Yep! How about your mom, Aiko-chan?

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:13.360
My mom's gone.

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:17.140
Ahh, don'tcha worry about it.

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:18.470
I'm sorry.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:19.490
It's alright.

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:22.410
I'm in the same situation.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:25.250
I don't have a father.

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:29.090
Yes, it was three years ago.

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:32.140
My father was a famous adventurer.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:36.550
He went to Cambodia to solve the mystery of the Angkor ruins.

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:40.220
A Japanese man was seen entering the jungle, but...

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:44.060
That was the last anyone heard of him.

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:47.910
No one knows whether he's alive or dead.

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:50.480
It's been three years, so he's probably...

00:09:52.390 --> 00:09:55.670
Don't give up hope, Nobu-chan. Yer father is alive.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:57.990
He <i>must</i>  be alive.

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:05.160
Thank you! I'll keep waiting, so Aiko-chan, you have to cheer up too.

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:08.120
Yeah, thanks.

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.440
What!?

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.530
What did you just say!?

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:39.820
I told you, Nobuko-chan's father is fine.

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:42.410
He was here for Parents' Day.

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:43.370
Right?

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:45.830
Then, that means...

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:48.790
Well, it means you were tricked.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:52.630
That dummy! I thought she knew the difference between a good lie and a bad lie!

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:57.670
Now I'm mad! Her tears had me completely fooled!

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:00.680
It's because Nobuko-chan's such a good actor.

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:04.140
Although, that was quite a performance, even for her.

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:09.180
Yep, I was almost moved to tears listening to her.

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:12.810
How can ya be so calm about it!?

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:15.230
W-Well, that's...

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:19.110
We've heard so many lies, we've gotten used to it.

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.780
Unforgivable...

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:27.830
I won't forgive her!

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:31.960
Hey, you!

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.000
Hold it right there!

00:11:36.750 --> 00:11:38.550
Didn't I tell ya to hold it!?

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:41.130
Hey! Stop! Stop! Stop!

00:11:43.670 --> 00:11:45.050
Ouch!

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:47.260
Ow ow! I'm sorry.

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:51.230
Senoo-san, what happened? Why were you running?

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:57.150
I see.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:02.110
She said her dad was dead. I can't accept that kind of lie.

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:06.370
Aiko-chan, what do you think of Nobuko-chan?

00:12:07.780 --> 00:12:11.330
I'm not sure. I don't think she's a bad girl, but...

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:13.330
Then why did she do that?

00:12:13.910 --> 00:12:15.180
What do you mean?

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:18.840
I mean, why did Nobuko-chan tell such a lie?

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:27.640
Ahhhh! I'm freaking furious!

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:31.140
And I can't figure out what Yuki-sensei was talkin' about either!

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:32.640
What's going on?

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:34.850
She was worse than this at school.

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:37.080
Even so, this is pretty scary.

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:39.110
She shouldn't have been tricked in the first place.

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:42.070
What did you say!?

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:45.160
Try sayin' that again!

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:47.240
Help me!

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.990
It just means Aiko-chan has a pure heart.

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:50.810
Right, Rika?

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:53.580
Yes yes, what she said!

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:55.540
It's good that ya understand.

00:12:57.910 --> 00:12:59.090
Scary...

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:07.180
What should I do now? Aiko-chan's mad at me.

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:12.350
Sorry!

00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:18.350
She won't forgive me no matter what I say.

00:13:20.970 --> 00:13:23.190
Where am I?

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:28.780
Ahhh! This is so irritatin'!

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:31.080
Today sucks! I'm goin' home!

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:40.210
Nobuko-chan.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:40.840
Eh?

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:45.090
Ah... Well... Good-bye!

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:48.970
Ow...

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:50.970
Nobuko-chan.

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:55.100
This way, this way!

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:01.400
How clumsy of her. Jeez....

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:03.940
What's this?

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:08.530
This, this! It looks interesting.

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:14.090
My name's Tatekawa Nobuo. I'm an elementary school student and a detective.

00:14:14.090 --> 00:14:17.710
If there are lost kittens in the north, I'll find and return them.

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:20.290
If there are gangsters in the south, I'll beat them up.

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:24.000
Look for me when you're in trouble, and I'll help you.

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:32.930
We've fallen into the evil Bone Bone Army's trap. It's a desperate situation!

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:36.600
It doesn't really matter, but what are you doing here, Professor Hadzuki?

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:39.900
Never mind that, the bomb's going to explode in one minute!

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:41.810
I know, but how...

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:45.570
I guess we can't use my inventions now.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:48.830
Hadzuki-chan, isn't this about you?

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:51.550
A scientist? Just like Hadzuki-chan.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:53.280
You... You think so?

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:55.950
Is this the end?

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:01.210
Y-You're...

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:02.880
Senoo Aiko.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:05.630
Boy Detective Tatekawa, I've come to save you!

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:06.990
It's Ai-chan.

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:08.380
Pretty good role.

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:11.090
Then, maybe I'm in there too!

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:13.300
Come on, hurry up.

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:14.010
Yeah!

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:14.970
Thank you.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.140
Oh no!

00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:21.600
We almost forgot Doremi.

00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:27.600
Why am I a dog?

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:40.870
Aiko-chan, thank you.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:45.040
Don't mention it, ain't we best friends?

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:49.170
It ends here.

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:53.100
Tatekawa Nobuo... Tatekawa, Tatekawa...

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:55.760
Yokokawa! Yokokawa Nobuko!

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:58.020
So it's about Nobuko-chan!

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:05.690
From this moment on, I'll be yer best friend, Nobu-chan.

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:07.180
Sure.

00:16:10.390 --> 00:16:12.820
W-W-What are you looking at?

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:15.280
Ain't we best friends?

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:18.240
So that's what she was writin' about.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:22.460
Looks like she was very happy that you'd be her best friend, Ai-chan.

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:24.960
Ai-chan, I think so too...

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.100
Got it.

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:27.880
But this is this.

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:30.550
I'm gonna go look for her.

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:33.090
I want to clear things up.

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:34.090
I'll go with you.

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:35.070
Why?

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:38.720
Because she made me into a dog!

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:42.790
Ah, that's it!

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:47.020
If Ai-chan looks for her, she'll just run away.

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:49.780
I have a better idea.

00:17:05.060 --> 00:17:07.460
Pretty Witchy Doremi-chi!

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:23.310
Pretty Witchy Hadzuki-chi!

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:39.120
Pretty Witchy Aiko-chi!

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:43.600
What're ya doin'? You're so slow!

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:45.330
Even if you say that...

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:47.290
Found her!

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:05.820
Pameruku Laruku Larilori Poppun!

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:09.060
Transform into Boy Detective Tatekawa!

00:18:13.310 --> 00:18:15.110
I actually don't want to do this but...

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:18.200
Pirika Pirilala Poporina Peperuto!

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:20.660
Transform into Doremi the loyal dog!

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:28.830
Paipai Ponpoi Puwapuwa Puu!

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:30.960
Transform into Professor Hadzuki!

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:34.960
Alright.

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.130
Let's go.

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:41.080
Yo, Nobuko-chan.

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:44.850
Who are you? I don't know you.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:46.520
What a greeting.

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:49.100
You created us, how could you forget?

00:18:51.010 --> 00:18:52.980
No way! Tatekawa?

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:57.190
The one and only, Boy Detective Tatekawa, in the flesh!

00:18:57.190 --> 00:18:59.530
I'm Professor Hadzuki, the genius scientist.

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:01.490
And this is Doremi the loyal dog.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:03.950
Anyway, Nobuko-chan.

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:07.870
Aiko-chan's very upset. We don't know what to do.

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:09.540
Do you know why?

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:12.380
Who're ya talkin' about?

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:14.590
How come I...!

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:16.590
So I was right.

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:20.150
It's all my fault.

00:19:20.150 --> 00:19:21.760
I made her angry.

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:24.930
Why did you make her angry?

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:28.520
My dad's alive, but I told her he's gone.

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:30.730
I think that's why Aiko-chan's so upset.

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:32.730
You regret it, don't you?

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:38.230
I see I see. Doremi, that's enough.

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:42.820
Well... Do you have anything to say to her?

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:45.240
N-N-Nobu-chan...

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:50.000
According to my investigation, Aiko-chan should be waiting for you.

00:19:51.030 --> 00:19:55.590
I think you should explain properly to Aiko-chan why you lied, Nobu-chan.

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:56.250
But...

00:19:56.250 --> 00:20:00.210
She'll listen to you. That's what best friends are for.

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:03.450
I'll go.

00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:06.930
I'll tell Aiko-chan everything and apologize.

00:20:07.460 --> 00:20:10.100
Aiko-chan's at the Maho-dou.

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:13.230
Thank you, Boy Detective Tatekawa.

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:18.650
Well, let's get to the Maho-dou before she does.

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:42.570
Sorry, I'm really sorry. I told such an awful lie.

00:20:42.570 --> 00:20:46.080
But when you said we were best friends...

00:20:46.080 --> 00:20:47.550
I was so happy.

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:50.810
I don't have any friends.

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:55.940
So I thought if I told you my dad was gone...

00:20:57.140 --> 00:21:01.820
I'd become closer to you because we'd be alike.

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:05.630
I see. I'm glad it's all out in the open, Nobu-chan.

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:08.950
But ya don't hafta worry 'bout me. I'm A-OK.

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:11.290
But please don't tell that kinda lie again.

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.560
Tryin' to cheer me up by lyin' ain't gonna make me happy.

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:15.000
I'm sorry.

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:16.730
It's alright.

00:21:16.990 --> 00:21:19.460
By the way, I read this.

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:22.130
It's really interestin'.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:24.470
Doremi the loyal dog is the best.

00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:25.260
Really?

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:26.340
Really, really.

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:30.010
I always thought Doremi-chan looked like somethin'.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:31.640
So she's a dog after all!

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:34.020
Who looks like a dog?

00:21:36.180 --> 00:21:37.980
Hey, Nobuko-chan...

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:40.940
Doremi the loyal dog isn't really a dog, right?

00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:42.610
She's actually under a magic spell, right?

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:45.450
Yes, she was actually a princess or something.

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:46.530
She's a dog.

00:21:47.560 --> 00:21:49.870
But she's not an ordinary dog.

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:53.160
Doremi the loyal dog can run ultra fast and understand human words.

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:54.910
And not only that...

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:02.710
It's here, it's here, it's here!

00:22:02.710 --> 00:22:04.840
The level 9 exam is finally here!

00:22:04.840 --> 00:22:07.680
If we pass, we can kiss being Ojamajos goodbye!

00:22:07.680 --> 00:22:12.310
However, I'm told to secretly look after Pop.

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:16.310
Why do I have to take care of my bratty little sister?

00:22:16.310 --> 00:22:19.940
I have to practice magic today!

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:22.680
Ojamajo Doremi!

00:22:22.680 --> 00:22:24.820
Aim for Level 9! The Witch Exam.
